.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
backend.hcl
*.tfvars.json

# emails.auto.tfvars holds personal addresses and this repo is public. It is the ONE input
# that cannot be committed, and it is a REQUIRED variable so its absence fails loudly.
emails.auto.tfvars

# terraform.tfvars is committed HERE on purpose, overriding `**/terraform.tfvars` in
# infra/.gitignore. Every value in it is already public, and its absence is what let a bare
# apply revert three settings to defaults that did not match the live account. See README.md.
!terraform.tfvars
